{
  "editions": [
    {
      "edition": "standard",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ οὖν Κύριος ἰδὼν τὴν ἁπλότητα αὐτῶν καὶ πᾶσαν νηπιότητα",
          "english_quote": "When the Lord saw their sincerity and their complete childlike innocence,",
          "issue": "The translation omits οὖν, losing the explicit consequential connection between the believers’ preceding conduct and the Lord’s response. “When” represents the participial construction but not this connective.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “Therefore, when the Lord saw their sincerity and their complete childlike innocence, …” Review the resulting sentence afresh before adopting it.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐνδεδυμένοι ⸢τὸ⸣ πνεῦμα ⸢τὸ ἅγιον⸣ τούτων τῶν παρθένων",
          "english_quote": "The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained; lowercase presentation here does not decide a later doctrinal identification.",
          "issue": "The note claims that house imagery is retained, but this selected clause contains clothing and virgins imagery, not house imagery. This imports an unsupported description into the explanation of this unit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace “The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained” with “The clothing and virgins imagery is retained.” Retain the distinction between editorial restorations and directly preserved text.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ πάντοτε σπλάγχνον ἔχοντες ἐπὶ πάντα ἄνθρωπον",
          "english_quote": "They had compassion for everyone.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition omits πάντοτε, “always,” from the compassion clause. The earlier occurrences of “always” modify other assertions and do not preserve this clause’s explicit emphasis.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “They always had compassion for everyone.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ οὖν Κύριος ἰδὼν τὴν ἁπλότητα αὐτῶν καὶ πᾶσαν νηπιότητα",
          "english_quote": "The Lord saw their sincerity and complete childlike innocence.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition omits οὖν, removing the explicit consequential connection to the preceding description of the believers.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “Therefore, the Lord saw their sincerity and complete childlike innocence.” Review this together with the following sentence so the Lord’s seeing and response remain connected.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐπλήθυνεν αὐτοὺς ἐν τοῖς κόποις τῶν χειρῶν αὐτῶν",
          "english_quote": "He made their work prosper",
          "issue": "The simplification drops the explicit reference to their hands. Although it retains the general idea of prospering work, it removes the source’s concrete description of their labor.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “He made them prosper in the work of their hands.” This wording still requires fresh review in the complete simplified sentence.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐνδεδυμένοι ⸢τὸ⸣ πνεῦμα ⸢τὸ ἅγιον⸣ τούτων τῶν παρθένων",
          "english_quote": "The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained; lowercase presentation here does not decide a later doctrinal identification.",
          "issue": "Independently of the standard edition, this note incorrectly describes house imagery as retained in the selected passage. Only clothing and virgins imagery occurs here.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace “The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained” with “The clothing and virgins imagery is retained.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "λέγω δὲ ὑμῖν τοῖς τοιούτοις οὖσιν ἐγὼ ὁ ἄγγελος τῆς μετανοίας· διαμείνατε τοιοῦτοι, καὶ οὐκ ἐξαλειφθήσεται τὸ σπέρμα ὑμῶν ἕως αἰῶνος.",
          "english_quote": "Preserve repentance conditions, confession, mercy and healing, and the declared foolishness, childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives.",
          "issue": "The unit-specific simplification metadata claims preservation of confession, mercy, healing, and a foolishness alternative that do not occur in this selected unit. The supplied report locates the foolishness case in S.9.xxii.4, not S.9.xxiv. This misstates the content and alternatives reviewed for this edition.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this inherited description with a unit-specific account of retaining the command to remain as described, the offspring promise, and the disclosed childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives. Do not attribute neighboring units’ content to this unit.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions require limited revision. The standard largely preserves the selected Greek; the simplified edition additionally loses explicit emphasis and concrete wording. Both retain servant terminology, contextual repentance, speaker identity, negations, and the difficult offspring promise. The childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed notes accurately reflect the supplied project report as edition-mediated alternatives; those alternatives do not justify replacing the declared working readings. This is a review against the supplied source and reports, not authentication of manuscripts or certification of exhaustive collation. Suggested replacements remain proposals requiring fresh review."
}
